NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - DAYLIGHT SAVING: in the weeks when London and New York change clocks on different dates (about 3 weeks in March, 1 in late October / early November) the PM auction is at 11:00 ET; the sheet always takes the 10:00 ET candle.
  - 10:00 US DATA: on days with a 10:00 ET release (ISM, JOLTS, Michigan, new home sales ...) the same candle also holds the release; the engine has no day rule that drops only the 10:00 releases, so those days stay in.
  - THE AUCTION'S RESULT: the fix price and the auction's rounds and volumes are not in the data; the candle stands in for the auction's net side.
  - THE STOP: the 10:00 candle's other extreme (the structure level), floored at two ticks and 0.25 x ATR; target 1.5 x that distance from the fill.
  - THE TIME EXIT: 13 bars of 15 minutes after the fill (exit_minutes 195, about 13:30 ET), not a clock time.
  - THE RANDOM CONTROL draws its entries anywhere in the nyam pass (09:30-11:00), not at the 10:15 close.
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, $4 a round turn, tick replay).
  - THE TEST DAYS (2025-07-01 on) ARE NOT READ by this sheet: build days only.

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - ONE session pass (nyam, 09:30-11:00): the cap of 1 trade is a cap of that window, which is the day's cap of the rule as far as the video's window lies inside it.
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).
  - The stop is the family's structure level of each entry (its size differs from trade to trade; the engine never puts it closer than two ticks or 0.25 ATR); `stop_val` is not used.

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
